---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Peach from '../components/Peach.astro';
import MoveArt from '../components/MoveArt.astro';
import { path } from '../lib/paths';
import { moves } from '../data/moves';
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="little-star">✳</span> A field guide for your behind</p><h1>Your butt called.<br/>It wants its<br/><span class="serif-word">job back.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Meet gluteal amnesia. The very real conversation behind a very silly name. Let’s get curious, get moving, and feel a little more connected.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={path('check-in/')}>Is my butt on a break? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={path('learn/')}>First, the butt basics <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="microcopy">Small moves. No shame. A few butt jokes.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-visual" id="hero-peach"><div class="field-note">FIG. 01 &nbsp; THE UNDEREMPLOYED GLUTE</div><Peach scene/><div class="peach-switch" aria-label="Illustration mood"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-peach="rest">On a break <span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-peach="move">Back in business <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><p class="illustration-note">A mascot. Not an anatomical model. Obviously.</p></div>
  </section>
  <div class="manifesto-strip"><div class="wrap flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3"><span>A GOOD BUTT IS A BUTT YOU LIVE IN.</span><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>MORE CAPACITY. LESS BODY ANXIETY.</span><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>EVERY BODY STARTS SOMEWHERE.</span></div></div>
  <section class="section wrap intro-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Let’s clear the air</p><h2>Not dead.<br/>Just <span class="serif-word">under-invited.</span></h2></div><div class="intro-text"><p class="large-copy">Your glutes help you stand up, climb stairs, and move through the world. Modern life gives them a lot of chair time.</p><p>“Dead butt syndrome” and “gluteal amnesia” are catchy labels for a mix of concerns about glute strength and coordination. Your muscles haven’t literally forgotten their job, and the nickname doesn’t tell us what’s causing your symptoms.</p><a class="text-link" href={path('learn/#what-is-it')}>What’s actually going on? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap pt-0"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose your own rear adventure</p><h2>Where are you starting?</h2></div><p>Curiosity is a perfectly good first move.</p></div><div class="entry-grid">
    <a class="entry-card card-peach" href={path('check-in/')}><span class="card-number">01 / NOTICE</span><span class="entry-icon" aria-hidden="true">?</span><h3>“Is this<br/>a me thing?”</h3><p>A gentle check-in for what you’re feeling. No diagnosis. No butt score.</p><span class="card-link">Check in with your body <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    <a class="entry-card card-sage" href={path('learn/')}><span class="card-number">02 / UNDERSTAND</span><span class="entry-icon" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><h3>“How did<br/>we get here?”</h3><p>Chairs, hips, hamstrings, and the surprisingly collaborative business of moving.</p><span class="card-link">Meet the whole team <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    <a class="entry-card card-butter" href={path('moves/')}><span class="card-number">03 / RECONNECT</span><span class="entry-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>“Okay.<br/>Let’s do something.”</h3><p>Simple ways to build strength and trust, from the ground up.</p><span class="card-link">Find your first move <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
  </div></section>
  <section class="chair-section"><div class="wrap section chair-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">The chair isn’t a villain. But it is very persuasive.</p><h2>We made a world<br/>that asks us<br/>to <span class="serif-word">sit it out.</span></h2><a class="text-link" href={path('learn/#sitting')}>The bigger picture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div><div class="day-timeline"><span>THE COMMUTE</span><i></i><span>THE DESK</span><i></i><span>THE COUCH</span></div><p class="large-copy">A workday can be busy without giving your body much variety.</p><p>That’s a design problem, not a character flaw. Break up long stretches where you can. Build strength over time. And yes, you’re still allowed to enjoy your chair.</p><div class="little-note"><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span><p>You don’t have to overhaul your life.<br/><strong>Start by interrupting one tiny bit of it.</strong></p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Give your glutes something to do</p><h2>A comeback in small moves.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={path('moves/')}>All six movement guides <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="move-grid">{moves.slice(0,3).map(move=><a class="move-card" href={path(`moves/${move.slug}/`)}><div class:list={['move-picture',`card-${move.color}`]}><MoveArt type={move.type}/><span class="move-time">{move.time}</span></div><div class="move-card-copy"><p class="eyebrow">{move.category}</p><h3>{move.name}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>{move.subtitle}</p></div></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="wrap"><div class="break-banner"><span class="break-flower" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><div><p class="eyebrow">A small intermission for your lower half</p><h2>Reading about moving?<br/>Try a little moving.</h2><p>Three easy minutes. A stable chair. Your own pace.</p></div><a class="button button-light" href={path('reset/')}>Take a movement break <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap faq-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Good questions. Honest answers.</p><h2>Let’s not make<br/>this <span class="serif-word">weirder.</span></h2><p>The jokes are loose.<br/>The claims should hold up.</p><a class="text-link" href={path('sources/')}>See our sources <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="faq-list">
    <details><summary>Is “dead butt” an actual diagnosis?<span>+</span></summary><p>It’s a popular nickname, used inconsistently. Weakness, changes in muscle coordination, gluteal tendon pain, and nerve-related symptoms need different explanations. A catchy label can’t distinguish them. <a href={path('learn/#what-is-it')}>Read the terminology guide.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>Does anterior pelvic tilt mean I’m broken?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. A forward-tilted pelvis is not a diagnosis of weak glutes or the cause of every ache. Posture varies. Focus on comfort and what you can do, and get persistent pain assessed. <a href={path('learn/#pelvis')}>Explore posture without panic.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need barefoot shoes?<span>+</span></summary><p>No purchase required. Some research suggests foot-strength benefits, with low-certainty evidence. There’s no demonstrated “dead butt” cure here. Comfortable shoes, foot exercises, and gradual changes are sensible starting points. <a href={path('learn/#feet')}>Read the footnotes.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>What if my butt is actually numb?<span>+</span></summary><p>Do not assume numbness is a sleepy muscle. Persistent or recurring numbness, spreading symptoms, or weakness deserves medical assessment. New saddle-area numbness or bladder/bowel changes needs emergency care. <a href={path('learn/#get-help')}>Know when to get help.</a></p></details>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<script>
  const scene = document.querySelector('#hero-peach');
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-peach]');
  buttons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    scene?.classList.toggle('is-awake', button.dataset.peach === 'move');
    buttons.forEach(item => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
  }));
</script>
